    {
      "file": "lib/minicrypto-pem.c",
      "function": "ptls_minicrypto_asn1_decode_private_key",
      "line": null,
      "code": "if (*decode_error == 0) {",
      "note": "The staged vulnerable source gates the parameters parse only on `*decode_error == 0`. It does not reject the already true `last_byte1 < byte_index` condition after OID parsing, so the next step subtracts `last_byte1 - byte_index` as an unsigned span and underflows.",
      "kind": "root_cause_function"
    },
    {
      "file": "lib/minicrypto-pem.c",
      "function": "ptls_minicrypto_asn1_decode_private_key",
      "line": 109,
      "code": "if (*decode_error == 0) {",
      "note": "The staged vulnerable source gates the parameters parse only on `*decode_error == 0`. It does not reject the already true `last_byte1 < byte_index` condition after OID parsing, so the next step subtracts `last_byte1 - byte_index` as an unsigned span and underflows.",
      "kind": "root_cause_line"
    },
    {
      "file": "lib/asn1.c",
      "function": "ptls_asn1_read_type",
      "line": null,
      "code": "uint8_t first_byte = bytes[0];",
      "note": "After the nested long-form length overread inflates the child return span, the parent recursive loop invokes `ptls_asn1_validation_recursive` again on `bytes + (35339 + heap_byte)` relative to the parameters sub-buffer, i.e. original allocation offset `35347 + heap_byte`. That pointer is far beyond the 1024-byte PEM backing allocation, and the next `ptls_asn1_read_type` immediately dereferences it here, matching the saved ASan heap-buffer-overflow.",
      "kind": "sink_function"
    },
